tion.\0A *\0A * This function sets up the verification of the MAC\0A * (message authentication code) of a byte string against an expected value.\0A *\0A * The sequence of operations to verify a MAC is as follows:\0A * -# Allocate an operation object which will be passed to all the functions\0A *    listed here.\0A * -# Initialize the operation object with one of the methods described in the\0A *    documentation for #psa_mac_operation_t, e.g. #PSA_MAC_OPERATION_INIT.\0A * -# Call psa_mac_verify_setup() to specify the algorithm and key.\0A * -# Call psa_mac_update() zero, one or more times, passing a fragment\0A *    of the message each time. The MAC that is calculated is the MAC\0A *    of the concatenation of these messages in order.\0A * -# At the end of the message, call psa_mac_verify_finish() to finish\0A *    calculating the actual MAC of the message and verify it against\0A *    the expected value.\0A *\0A * If an error occurs at any step after a call to psa_mac_verify_setup(), the\0A * operation will need to be reset by a call to psa_mac_abort(). The\0A * application may call psa_mac_abort() at any time after the operation\0A * has been initialized.\0A *\0A * After a successful call to psa_mac_verify_setup(), the application must\0A * eventually terminate the operation through one of the following methods:\0A * - A successful call to psa_mac_verify_finish().\0A * - A call to psa_mac_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation The operation object to set up. It must have\0A *                          been initialized as per the documentation for\0A *                          #psa_mac_operation_t and not yet in use.\0A * \5Cparam key               Identifier of the key to use for the operation. It\0A *                          must remain valid until the operation terminates.\0A *                          It must allow the usage\0A *                          PSA_KEY_USAGE_VERIFY_MESSAGE.\0A * \5Cparam alg               The MAC algorithm to compute (\5Cc PSA_